<!-- 01 ANSWER-FIRST -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · The short answer</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">A Samsung that tumbles but won't heat is usually a choked vent.</h2>

    <p><strong>When a Samsung dryer runs but won't heat, the leading cause is a restricted exhaust vent, not a broken part. A clogged vent traps heat, the dryer overheats, and Samsung's protection either blows a thermal fuse or throws an HE/hE overheat code and cuts the heat. After the vent, the common failed parts are the heating element and the thermistor. On a gas Samsung, it's a weak igniter, a gas-valve coil, or the flame sensor. Clean the lint filter and the full exhaust vent first — it fixes most no-heat calls and removes a genuine fire hazard. If it still won't heat on a clear vent, it's a diagnostic. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</strong></p>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Why the vent comes first — and fast:</strong> the same lint-clogged vent that stops your Samsung from heating is a leading cause of house fires. The U.S. Fire Administration counts about 15,600 dryer fires a year, and the NFPA finds failure to clean the dryer and its venting is the number-one factor. A dryer running hot or showing HE is worth clearing the same day.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 CAUSES -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Why a Samsung dryer stops heating</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The causes, in the order our techs find them.</h2>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Restricted vent → overheat / HE code (most common)</h3>
      <p>A lint-clogged filter or exhaust duct chokes the airflow, the dryer runs too hot, and the thermal fuse blows or an <strong>HE/hE</strong> code appears as the heat is cut for safety. This is the first thing to rule out on any Samsung no-heat call, and it's usually a free fix.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Heating element (electric models)</h3>
      <p>The element is the coil that heats the air on an electric Samsung. When it burns open, the dryer tumbles with no heat and no code. It's tested for continuity and replaced — a tech job inside the cabinet.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Thermistor / thermal fuse</h3>
      <p>The thermistor tells the control the air temperature; when it misreads, it can cut heat or trigger a false HE. The thermal fuse is a one-time safety device that blows on overheat and doesn't reset — if it's open, the dryer won't heat until it's replaced <em>and</em> the vent that caused it is cleared.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Gas models — igniter, valve coils, flame sensor</h3>
      <p>On a gas Samsung, no-heat usually means the burner isn't lighting: a weak igniter, failed gas-valve solenoid coils, or a bad flame (radiant) sensor. The tell is an igniter that glows and then goes out without the gas lighting. Gas components are a tech job — never DIY the gas valve.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>One 240V leg lost (electric)</h3>
      <p>An electric dryer runs on a 240V double breaker. If only one leg trips, the drum still tumbles and the lights work, but there's no heat. Reset both halves of the breaker before assuming a part failed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 SAFE FIX -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · What you can safely check</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Clear the vent, check the breaker.</h2>

    <ol class="diag-list">
      <li><strong>Clean the lint filter and the full vent.</strong> Pull and wash the filter, disconnect and clear the flexible hose behind the dryer, and confirm the exterior flap opens. This fixes most no-heat and HE calls — and removes the fire hazard.</li>
      <li><strong>Reset both breaker legs (electric).</strong> Flip the 240V double breaker fully off and on. A single tripped leg tumbles without heat.</li>
      <li><strong>Confirm gas supply (gas).</strong> Make sure the gas is on and other gas appliances work. Do not touch the gas valve or line.</li>
      <li><strong>Power-cycle for a stuck HE code.</strong> Unplug for a minute after cleaning the vent, then restart.</li>
      <li><strong>Watch whether HE or no-heat returns.</strong> Gone after a vent cleaning = it was airflow. Returns on a clear vent = a failed part.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Where to stop:</strong> vent cleaning and the breaker check are safe and fix a large share of Samsung no-heat calls. Do not open the dryer cabinet to test the heating element, thermistor, or thermal fuse, and never disturb the gas line or gas valve on a gas dryer. A no-heat that survives a full vent cleaning is the handoff point.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 TECH + LINKS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">04 · When it's a tech job</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Clean vent, still cold? Now it's a diagnostic.</h2>

    <p>When the vent is verified clear and the Samsung still won't heat — or HE keeps returning — the fault is inside: a burned-out heating element, a misreading thermistor, an open thermal fuse (plus the vent that blew it), or on gas the igniter, valve coils, or flame sensor. Our techs verify the vent first, then test the heating circuit and replace only the failed part. These are among the more affordable dryer repairs, so a no-heat Samsung is usually well worth fixing. <strong>$89 residential diagnostic, waived with the repair.</strong></p>

    <p>More help: the general <a href="/services/dryer-repair/not-heating/">dryer not heating</a> guide (all brands) and the <a href="/services/dryer-repair/error-codes/">dryer error codes</a> reference, including where HE fits among Samsung's codes. If your dryer takes multiple cycles, that's <a href="/services/dryer-repair/takes-too-long/">dryer takes too long</a>, usually the same restricted vent. A chronically clogged vent deserves a dedicated <a href="/services/dryer-vent-repair/">dryer vent</a> cleaning. Brand coverage: <a href="/brands/samsung-dryer-repair/">Samsung dryer repair</a>. Same-day across <a href="/los-angeles/dryer-repair/">Los Angeles</a>, <a href="/beverly-hills/dryer-repair/">Beverly Hills</a>, and <a href="/irvine/dryer-repair/">Irvine</a> in most cases. <a href="/book/">Book online</a> or call {phone}.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 FAQ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">05 · FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Samsung dryer not heating: common questions.</h2>

